// failure.proto — THE FAILURE VOCABULARY A SURFACE DRAWS, and the typed
// evidence every failure carries.
//
// One closed oneof naming every way work can fail ON ITS OWN, plus the typed
// evidence each kind carries. It is a VOCABULARY FILE, not a component file:
// nothing here describes a card, a row or a cell. Surfaces embed FailureKind in
// their own resolved props and render it their own way — the feed's card
// (feed.proto), the footer's row (footer.proto), the roster's notice
// (sidebar.proto). One vocabulary, per-surface carriers, exactly as
// tokens.proto is one economics vocabulary behind several resolved views.
//
// WHY IT IS frontend.v1 AND NOT agentrepl.v1. This vocabulary used to live in
// `agentrepl/v1/shared.proto` and serve two jobs at once: the account a command
// refusal carried back, and the account a spontaneous failure was drawn from.
// Serving both meant `frontend/v1/feed.proto` had to IMPORT `agentrepl/v1` so
// that FailureCardView could name a kind — a MODEL package importing a BOUNDARY
// package, backwards under the ownership scheme in
// DESIGN-protobuf-surfaces.md. The two jobs are now two vocabularies. What
// ANSWERS a call is an arm of that call's own `<Method>Error` in agentrepl.v1.
// What HAPPENS ON ITS OWN — a session dying mid-turn, a rate limit, a shim
// crash — is not an answer to anything, arrives on the push stream, and is
// named here.
//
// THE EVIDENCE MESSAGES ARE DECLARED ONCE, HERE, AND BOTH SIDES NAME THEM.
// Several failures can genuinely be either an event or an answer — an SDK query
// that terminated, a conversation that would not resume, a machinery failure
// nothing could classify. Nothing is duplicated for them: there is ONE
// SessionResumeFailure on the wire, named by a drawn arm below and by a called
// arm in agentrepl.v1, and the ARM is what says whether this instance is an
// answer or an event. agentrepl.v1 may import frontend.v1; the reverse is the
// import this file exists to remove.
//
// WHY KINDS AND NOT A CLASS PLUS A STRING. A failure is a CONDITION, and a
// condition is what a oneof is for. Naming the kind on the wire means a
// consumer that meets an unfamiliar failure fails to match it instead of
// silently rendering it as something else, and it means each kind carries the
// evidence that kind actually has rather than a shared free-text field that
// every producer packs differently and every consumer parses differently.
//
// THE MACHINERY/VENDOR DISTINCTION IS CARRIED BY THE ARM, not by a second
// field. Every kind belongs to exactly one side — agent-repl's own machinery
// failing, or the vendor refusing or concluding the work — and each arm's
// comment states its side and the workspace color that side resolves to. A
// separate class field would be a fact derivable from the arm, which is a fact
// that can disagree with the arm.

